    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0353" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13189: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong
                                Kong</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-11T13:00:00+08:00">June 11, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 11—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In continuation of my telegram of this date,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d464-f1"/>
                    Japanese Consul General expressed the informal and strictly confidential opinion
                    that <pb facs="0354" n="350" xml:id="pg350"/> bombing would continue in Canton
                    and other places in South China thus making highly advisable identification of
                    all American property.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
